ixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:3:每个参考题描述包含：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:4:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:5:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:6:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"22806e14\" lines=\"23-37\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:11:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:12:Mark the center of each odd-sized solid square with the plus marker color, erasing the marker only when it is outside the marked-center field.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:13:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:14:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:15:- The dominant color is background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:16:- Exactly two foreground colors are present: one unique 3x3 plus marker and one color forming separated solid square objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:17:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:18:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:19:- For every non-marker 4-connected object, assert it is a solid square.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:20:- If the square side length is odd, recolor its center pixel to the plus marker color; even-sided squares stay unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:21:- Preserve the plus marker when its center lies inside the bounding box of the odd-square centers; otherwise erase it to background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:22:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:23:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:24:- Odd-sided solid squares have a single visible center pixel, and the plus supplies the color used to identify those centers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:25:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:26:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:27:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:28:<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\" lines=\"42-56\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:29:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:30:Fill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:31:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:32:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:33:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:34:- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:35:- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:36:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:37:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:38:- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:39:- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:40:- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:41:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:42:Key insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:43:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:44:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:45:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:46:<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"4a1cacc2\" lines=\"8-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:47:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:48:Fill the rectangle from the lone foreground pixel to its nearest grid corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:49:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:50:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:51:- The grid is a uniform background field with exactly one foreground pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:52:- The foreground pixel's color is the color used for all added pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:53:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:54:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:55:- Find the grid corner with the smallest Manhattan distance to the foreground pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:56:- Recolor every pixel in the inclusive axis-aligned rectangle bounded by that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:57:  corner and the foreground pixel to the foreground color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:58:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:59:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:60:- The single pixel is one corner of the rectangle; the opposite corner is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:61:  nearest corner of the whole canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:62:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:63:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:64:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:65:<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"182e5d0f\" lines=\"89-103\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:66:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:67:Move each gray marker along its green path until it reaches the cell next to a black-green-black gate, erasing the path behind it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:68:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:69:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:70:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:71:- Foreground components are made from a path color, a paired gate-end color, and single marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:72:- A gate is a straight end-center-end motif whose center has the path color and whose two ends share the gate-end color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:73:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:74:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:75:- In every 4-connected foreground component with exactly one marker and one gate, erase the marker and all path-color pixels except the gate center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:76:- Place the marker on the unique path-color pixel adjacent to the gate center but not between the two gate ends.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:77:- Components without both a marker and a gate stay unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:78:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:79:Key insight: The black-green-black motif marks the stopping gate; the gray marker consumes the connected green path until it rests on the path cell immediately beside that gate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:80:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:81:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:82:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:83:<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"833966f4\" lines=\"8-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:84:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:85:Swap the upper two-pixel segment and the lower two-pixel segment around the fixed center pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:86:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:87:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:88:- The grid is a 5x1 vertical column of individual colored pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:89:- The middle pixel is a separator between two same-size two-pixel segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:90:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:91:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:92:- Keep the middle pixel in place.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:93:- Reverse the order of the two pixels above the middle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:94:- Reverse the order of the two pixels below the middle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:95:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:96:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:97:- The transformation is local vertical order reversal on each side of the center, not a color-specific rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:98:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:99:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:100:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:101:<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"38007db0\" lines=\"9-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:102:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:103:Extract the unique cell from each lattice row into a single-column lattice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:104:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:105:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:106:- Grid divided into equal square cells by uniform gridlines of color L.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:107:- Cell interiors filled with bg; each cell has an inner sprite pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:108:- Each row of cells has exactly one cell with a unique pattern; the rest are copies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:109:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:110:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:111:- For each lattice row, find the cell whose inner pattern appears exactly once (the \"odd one out\").\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:112:- Construct a single-column lattice preserving the original row heights, containing only the unique cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:113:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:114:Key insight: The task is per-row \"odd one out\" — every cell in a row is identical except one oddball, which must be extracted.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:115:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:116:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:117:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:118:<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"800d221b\" lines=\"7-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:119:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:120:Recolor a path-network by adjacent seed regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:121:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:122:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:123:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:124:- Path color P forms a thin orthogonal network with a solid square hub (NxN).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:125:- Seed colors appear in colored regions (non-bg, non-P) adjacent to path branches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:126:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:127:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:128:- Infer P as the non-bg color whose largest component is most network-like.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:129:- Find the largest solid k×k all-P square (the hub); exclude it from recoloring.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:130:- Recolor each path branch to the seed-region color it touches most.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:131:- Recolor the hub center pixel to the seed whose branches touch the hub most.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:132:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:133:Key insight: The hub stays uncolored; branches inherit color from adjacent seed regions by adjacency count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:134:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:135:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:136:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:137:<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"17b866bd\" lines=\"49-67\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:138:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:139:Move each marker from a lattice corner gap into the adjacent enclosed 12-pixel cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:140:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:141:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:142:- The grid is a repeated teal lattice around black 12-pixel cavities.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:143:- A marker is a non-black pixel placed at the northwest corner gap of one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:144:  complete 5x5 lattice tile; the marker may itself be teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:145:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:146:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:147:- For every marked northwest corner gap, clear that marker to black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:148:- Fill the 12 black pixels in the tile immediately down-right of the marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:149:  with the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:150:- Leave the rest of the lattice unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:151:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:152:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:153:- The apparent isolated markers are control pixels for the adjacent cavity;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:154:  teal markers are recognized as extra teal pixels occupying a gap that the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:155:  periodic lattice template says should be black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:156:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:157:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:158:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:159:<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"fc7cae8d\" lines=\"9-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:160:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:161:Align a central rectangle to two colored frame-edge controls via rotation/reflection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:162:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:163:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:164:- bg grid with two solid-colored border edges (distinct non-bg colors).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:165:- A central filled rectangle with 1px colored guide edges on two sides, colors matching the frame controls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:166:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:167:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:168:- Rotate/mirror the object so its guide edges face the same sides as the matching frame controls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:169:- Crop off the 1px guide edges from aligned sides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:170:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:171:Key insight: Guide-edge colors encode target frame sides; the correct dihedral transform matches both simultaneously.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:172:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:173:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:174:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:175:<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5ad8a7c0\" lines=\"10-24\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:176:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:177:Connect the innermost mirrored marker pair(s) by filling their horizontal span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:178:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:179:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:180:- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:181:- Each foreground row contains exactly two foreground pixels mirrored across the vertical center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:182:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:183:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:184:- Find the foreground row pair(s) with the smallest horizontal gap between the two markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:185:- Fill every pixel between those two markers in each selected row with the foreground color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:186:- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:187:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:188:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:189:- Wider marker pairs are context; the closest marker pair(s) show the unresolved horizontal segment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:190:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:191:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:192:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:193:<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5b37cb25\" lines=\"59-73\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:194:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:195:Fill each plus-shaped background notch with the color of the frame side it opens toward.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:196:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:197:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:198:- A one-cell-thick rectangular frame has four solid-colored sides and neutral corner pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:199:- The frame interior contains a dominant background color and one foreground object color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:200:- Some object boundaries contain five-pixel plus-shaped background notches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:201:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:202:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:203:- Find every background plus whose opposite side is supported by foreground object pixels and whose open side faces one frame side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:204:- Recolor the five pixels of that plus with the color of the facing frame side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:205:- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:206:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:207:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:208:The frame side colors are direction labels for the open notches in the foreground object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:209:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:210:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:211:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:212:<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"689c358e\" lines=\"72-88\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:213:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:214:Mark each arrow-like sprite's pointed frame endpoint with its color and the opposite endpoint black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:215:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:216:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:217:- The grid has a one-pixel solid rectangular frame around a dominant interior background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:218:- Inside the frame are monochrome six-pixel sprites shaped as asymmetric T arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:219:- Each sprite has a length-4 bar and a length-3 crossbar one cell closer to the pointed end.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:220:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:221:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:222:- For each sprite, follow its bar axis from the shorter end to the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:223:- Paint that frame endpoint with the sprite color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:224:- Paint the opposite endpoint on the same row or column black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:225:- Leave the interior background, sprites, and all other frame pixels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:226:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:227:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:228:- The direction is encoded by the crossbar's off-center position: the nearer end is the pointing end.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:229:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:230:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:231:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:232:<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"42f83767\" lines=\"23-39\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:233:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:234:Expand the lower color grid by replacing each pixel with its matching top stencil.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:235:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:236:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:237:The input has a top legend and a lower dense color grid, separated by blank rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:238:The legend contains left-to-right 2x2 color swatches and, to their right,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:239:the same number of square neutral-color stencil masks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:240:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:241:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:242:Pair the swatches and stencil masks by left-to-right order. For every pixel in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:243:the lower color grid, paste the paired stencil mask as one output block,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:244:recoloring the mask pixels with that pixel's color and leaving mask holes as bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:245:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:246:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:247:The lower grid is not copied directly; it is an index grid whose colors select\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:248:the stencil shape from the legend, so each input pixel becomes one square block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:249:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:250:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:251:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:252:<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"28a6681f\" lines=\"8-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:253:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:254:Simulate water pixels falling under gravity into basins formed by colored obstacles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:255:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:256:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:257:- bg = 0. Water pixels = color 1 (blue).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:258:- Other colors form static solid structures (walls, steps, containers).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:259:- Water starts in unstable positions above or beside basins.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:260:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:261:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:262:- Each water pixel falls straight down through bg cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:263:- When blocked below, it slides diagonally through the unique open side cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:264:- When resting on a surface, it slides horizontally toward the nearest gap where it can fall again.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:265:- Process repeats until no water pixel moves.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:266:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:267:Key insight: Water seeks the deepest reachable basin via diagonal and horizontal sliding, not just vertical fall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:268:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:269:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:270:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:271:<reference_puzzle index=\"15\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"abc82100\" lines=\"70-86\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:272:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:273:Use local source-target-pattern examples to replace matching source pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:274:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:275:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:276:- Black background with isolated colored pixels and teal (8) pattern components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:277:- A rule example is a 4-neighbor colored pair source->target whose continued\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:278:  direction reaches an anchor touching a teal pattern component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:279:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:280:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:281:- For each rule example, copy that teal component onto every other pixel of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:282:  source.color, recoloring the copied component to target.color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:283:- Translation maps the rule anchor onto the source pixel being replaced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:284:- Remove teal components and all pixels used by rule examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:285:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:286:Key insight: The two adjacent colored pixels define the color substitution and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:287:the anchor point; the nearby teal component is the stencil that gets recolored.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:288:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:289:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:290:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:291:<reference_puzzle index=\"16\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"35ab12c3\" lines=\"73-88\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:292:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:293:Complete outlined shapes and carry attached shadow pixels along their edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:294:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:295:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:296:- bg = background. Each active color marks vertices of an 8-direction aligned outline.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:297:- A start vertex can have adjacent non-bg, different-colored shadow pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:298:- Other colored pixels may be distractors unless they lie on valid drawable edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:299:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:300:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:301:- For each color, order its pixels by polar angle around their centroid to form a cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:302:- Draw only horizontal, vertical, or 45-degree edges whose interiors are clear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:303:- From the chosen start vertex, copy adjacent shadow offsets along each drawable edge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:304:  when the parallel path is in bounds and clear.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:305:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:306:Key insight: The main outline is reconstructed first, then the start vertex's neighbor offsets define parallel shadow strokes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:307:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:308:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:309:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:310:<reference_puzzle index=\"17\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"de809cff\" lines=\"86-103\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:311:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:312:Turn black dents in two colored regions into marked opposite-color patches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:313:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:314:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:315:- Black background with two large foreground colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:316:- The large regions contain small black dents and a few one-cell color specks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:317:  or protrusions along region boundaries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:318:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:319:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:320:- Locally clean the two foreground regions: isolated specks become black, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:321:  one-cell protrusions surrounded by the other region take that region's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:322:- Each original black dent whose cleaned 3x3 neighborhood is mostly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:323:  foreground color becomes the center of a 3x3 patch in the opposite color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:324:- The dent center itself is recolored teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:325:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:326:Key insight: The teal pixels mark the original black defects; the surrounding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:327:3x3 patch uses the other foreground color, after first removing boundary noise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:328:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:329:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:330:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:331:<reference_puzzle index=\"18\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"4c416de3\" lines=\"99-118\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:332:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:333:Replicate a pre-drawn corner pattern to every other marker-bearing corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:334:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:335:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:336:- bg = most frequent color. Hollow 0-frames (possibly partial L-shapes); each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:337:  frame-corner cell is either 0 or a painted (non-bg, non-0) color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:338:- >= 1 'source' corner: the pattern is already drawn (one color, both outward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:339:  cells and an inward-diagonal trail).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:340:- Other corners: a single colored pixel on the inward diagonal at the pattern's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:341:  deepest (k,k) offset; the pixel's color is that corner's target color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:342:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:343:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:344:- Extract the canonical (TL-oriented) pattern from any source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:345:- For each non-source corner whose marker cell is colored, paint the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:346:  pattern rotated to that corner's orientation, using the marker's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:347:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:348:Key insight: the pattern is symmetric about the corner's inward-diagonal axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:349:(canonical dr == dc), so it reflects cleanly across all four corner orientations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:350:Painting uses each target's OWN marker color, not the source color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:351:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:352:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:353:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:354:<reference_puzzle index=\"19\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ad3b40cf\" lines=\"72-87\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:355:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:356:Mirror the smallest non-axis foreground color across the full straight axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:357:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:358:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:359:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:360:- One foreground color forms exactly one full row, column, main diagonal, or anti-diagonal reflection axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:361:- The remaining foreground colors include a unique least-populated color to copy.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:362:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:363:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:364:- Preserve the input grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:365:- Select every pixel of the unique smallest non-axis foreground color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:366:- Reflect those pixels across the full straight axis and paint the reflected positions with the same color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:367:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:368:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:369:- The axis color marks the mirror line, while the color population chooses which set of objects is duplicated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:370:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:371:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:372:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:373:<reference_puzzle index=\"20\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9841fdad\" lines=\"15-39\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:374:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:375:Expand the colored runs from the left reference panel into the blank right panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:376:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:377:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:378:- A uniform rectangular frame surrounds the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:379:- One full-height divider of the frame color splits a left reference panel\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:380:  from a blank right panel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:381:- Both panels have one background margin column on each side of their active\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:382:  columns; the left active columns contain two-column endpoint slots, possibly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:383:  connected by same-color horizontal runs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:384:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:385:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:386:- Keep the original grid and paint only in the right panel's active columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:387:- A source run exactly matching the left endpoint slot is copied to the left\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:388:  two columns of the right active span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:389:- A source run exactly matching the right endpoint slot is copied to the right\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:390:  two columns of the right active span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:391:- A source run connecting the endpoint slots is stretched across the entire\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:392:  right active span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:393:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:394:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:395:The left panel is a compressed legend for the right panel: endpoint markers\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:396:stay two pixels wide, while connectors between endpoints expand to fill the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:397:distance between them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:398:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:399:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:400:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:401:你的任务：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:402:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:403:创新方式包括但不限于：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:404:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:405:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:406:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:407:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:408:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:409:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:410:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:411:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:412:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:413:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:414:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:415:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:416:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:417:请一次性生成5个`<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:418:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:419:注意事项：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:420:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:421:2. 关于\"计算\"的边界：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:422:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:423:   - **禁止使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算（取模） / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算都是禁止使用的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:424:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id和颜色亮度是禁止使用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:425:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:426:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:427:6. 新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:428:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:429:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:430:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\"结构层数\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\"找到缺口在哪一侧\"、\"数出像素个数\"、\"识别哪个对象最大\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:431:   - ✗ 伪两层：\"找到缺口方向\"→\"把东西推到对面\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:432:   - ✓ 真两层：\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\"→\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:433:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:434:   如果你发现自己写出的题只是\"对每个对象，根据它的某个属性做某变换\"的单步规则，请引入一个需要主动推理的前置步骤。**用堆叠 tie-break 规则或复杂数学公式来\"加难度\"是劣解；用多一层需要归纳的结构嵌套来\"加难度\"才是好解**。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:435:10. 在符合ARC题目和提示词要求的基础上，鼓励尝试创新规则为多层结构的题目，不局限于两层，可以创新三层或四层结构的题目，但不可为了多结构层数违背要求。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:436:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:437:生成后对生成的题执行以下四项审查（审查内容不需要保存到文件）：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:438:1. 原创性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:439:  新题不可与上述参考题相同或类似，不可只是替换颜色、方向、对象类型等表层要素。判断标准：新题的核心推理路径应与任何一道参考题不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:440:2. 确定性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:441:  规则完全确定，同一输入只能产生唯一输出，每一步操作都有明确定义。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:442:3. 可实现性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:443:  所有必要细节都已给出——对象如何生成、如何识别、如何变换、边界情况如何处理，读完描述后可以直接写代码。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:444:4. ARC 合规性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:445:  网格尺寸合理（≤30×30），使用颜色不超过 10 种，规则复杂度适中，人类能从 3-5 个样例中发现规律。没有使用上述注意事项第二条禁止使用的复杂计算。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/prompt.md:446:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:1:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:2:- `description`：根据封闭区域内\"种子色块\"的形状，从外部颜色图例中匹配对应模板，用图例颜色填充该封闭区域。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:3:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:4:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:5:  - 背景为 Black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:6:  - 网格上方有一行颜色图例区：若干小型彩色图案（如 L 形、T 形、直线等），每个图案使用不同颜色绘制，图案之间用 Black 间隔。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:7:  - 网格下方的主区域中，有若干由 Grey 像素围成的封闭矩形区域（Grey 围墙厚度为 1 像素）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:8:  - 每个封闭区域内部有一个小型 Maroon 色块（\"种子\"），其形状与上方图例中某个图案的形状完全一致（像素级匹配，仅颜色不同）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:9:  - 封闭区域内部除种子色块外其余像素为 Black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:10:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:11:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:12:  - 第一步：对每个封闭区域，提取其内部 Maroon 种子色块的形状（相对像素坐标集合）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:13:  - 第二步：在上方图例中找到形状完全匹配该种子的图案，记录该图案的颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:14:  - 第三步：将该封闭区域内所有 Black 像素（不含 Grey 围墙）填充为匹配到的图例颜色；同时将种子的 Maroon 像素也替换为该颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:15:  - Grey 围墙和图例区保持不变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:16:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/9/des.md:17:- `Key insight`：种子色块的形状是查找图例